@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title Activity - disasterrecovery/DrPlan
skinparam activity {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  diamondBackgroundColor #e2e8f0
  diamondBorderColor #1d4ed8
  diamondFontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
  barColor #1d4ed8
}
start
partition "Observe and Bind" {
:Start from shared flow\nshared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg;
:Read desired DrPlan spec, tracked status, and\ndelete intent;
if ("Tracked or explicit OCI identity present?") then (yes)
:Get the current OCI resource via GetDrPlan;
else (no)
:Resolve an existing OCI resource through\nListDrPlans using filters drProtectionGroupId,\ndisplayName, type, drPlanId;
:Create the OCI resource via CreateDrPlan when\nno reusable match is found;
:Persist the resolved or created OCI identity\ninto status;
endif
}
if ("Delete requested?") then (yes)
partition "Delete" {
:Delete path uses DeleteDrPlan with required\nvia GetDrPlan or ListDrPlans to DELETED\nconfirmation;
:Confirm deletion via GetDrPlan or ListDrPlans\nuntil OCI reaches DELETED;
if ("Delete cleanup and finalizer release succeed?") then (yes)
:Remove the finalizer after delete completion;
else (no)
:Stay blocked until cleanup or finalizer\nrelease succeeds;
endif
}
stop
else (no)
partition "Lifecycle Classification" {
if ("OCI state in retryable set?") then (yes)
:Request requeue while OCI remains in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING;
stop
endif
if ("OCI state is outside success targets?") then (yes)
:Return an unsuccessful reconcile result until\nOCI reaches ACTIVE, INACTIVE;
stop
endif
}
partition "Ready and Drift Handling" {
:Compare live OCI state against the\nrepo-authored mutation surface;
if ("Force-new or conflicting drift detected?") then (yes)
:Reject drift before OCI mutation for force-new\nfields drProtectionGroupId, sourcePlanId, type;
stop
endif
if ("Supported mutable drift detected?") then (yes)
:Apply UpdateDrPlan only for mutable fields\ndefinedTags, displayName, freeformTags,\nplanGroups;
else (no)
:Skip the no-op mutation path;
endif
:Run provider helper hooks\ncreate=tfresource.CreateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForWorkRequestWithErrorHandling\nentity=drplan action=CREATED;\nupdate=tfresource.UpdateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForWorkRequestWithErrorHandling\nentity=drplan action=UPDATED;\ndelete=tfresource.DeleteResource when the\nmatching field-driven path executes;
:Apply explicit follow-up semantics\ncreate=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;\nupdate=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;\ndelete=GetDrPlan/ListDrPlans confirm-delete;
:Return success for the ACTIVE, INACTIVE\nsuccess state;
:Project required status and finalizer policy\nretain-until-confirmed-delete;
:Requeue on provisioning, updating, terminating;
}
endif
stop
note right
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg
Start from the shared reconcile activity and
specialize provider-backed CRUD, wait, and
status-projection details here.
Controller-local activity diagrams add
list-lookup hints, secret policies, delete
handling, and open formal gaps.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers specialize the shared reconcile path
with formal runtime ownership.
service: disasterrecovery
slug: drplan
kind: DrPlan
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update
UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;
update=GetWorkRequest -> GetDrPlan;
delete=GetDrPlan/ListDrPlans confirm-delete
supported drift: definedTags, displayName,
freeformTags, planGroups
reject before mutate: force-new fields
drProtectionGroupId, sourcePlanId, type
create-only fields: none
list lookup: oci_disaster_recovery_dr_plans
filters drProtectionGroupId, displayName, type,
drPlanId; exact drProtectionGroupId plus
displayName and type unique match; tracked
rereads and delete confirmation can additionally
narrow by drPlanId
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
DrPlan create and update are work-request-backed
and resume through status.async.current as the
canonical in-flight tracker.
List responses expose DrPlanSummary items only,
so the runtime rereads GetDrPlan before status
projection or mutable drift checks that depend
on planGroups or sourcePlanId.
Create ignores spec.planGroups because
CreateDrPlanDetails does not accept planGroups;
in-place plan group edits are published only
through UpdateDrPlanDetails.
The resource-local update builder strips
read-only group and step fields from GetDrPlan
before diffing so service-owned metadata does
not cause perpetual updates.
Refresh, verify, plan execution, and other
disaster recovery helper families remain out of
scope for this controller-backed runtime.
end note
@enduml
